### 8.3 Swagger YAML (OpenAPI Spec)
# File available at: docs/swagger.yaml


###############################################################################
# NOTES
###############################################################################
#
# Certificate Validity Recommendations:
# - CA Root: 10 years (3650 days) - Rarely changed
# - CA Intermediate: 5 years (1825 days)
# - Server Certificates: 1 year (365 days) - Industry standard
# - Client Certificates (IoT): 3 years (1095 days) - Harder to renew
# - Client Certificates (Apps): 1 year (365 days) - Easier to renew
#
# Key Size Recommendations:
# - CA: 4096 bits (maximum security)
# - Server: 2048 bits (good balance)
# - Client: 2048 bits (good balance)
# - IoT (low power): Consider ECC instead of RSA
#
# Common Name (CN) Guidelines:
# - CA: Descriptive name (e.g., "Company Root CA 2024")
# - Server: MUST match DNS name (e.g., "mqtt.example.com")
# - Client: Unique identifier (e.g., "device-001", "user@email.com")
#
# Subject Alternative Names (SANs):
# - Always include the CN in SANs
# - Add all domain variations (www, non-www, subdomains)
# - Wildcards supported: *.example.com
# - Note: *.example.com does NOT cover example.com (add both)
#
# Country Codes (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2):
# - IT (Italy), US (United States), GB (United Kingdom)
# - DE (Germany), FR (France), ES (Spain), JP (Japan)
# - MUST be exactly 2 uppercase letters
#
# File Locations:
# - CA: certs/ca/ca-cert.pem, certs/ca/ca-key.pem
# - Server: certs/servers/{uuid}/cert.pem, key.pem
# - Client: certs/clients/{uuid}/cert.pem, key.pem
#
###############################################################################